4.8 The symbols of the functions of the oil ports should be clearly marked near all the connecting oil ports of the components. Except for special regulations, the symbols of the oil ports are as follows:
P—pressure oil port;
T—return oil port;
A, B—working oil ports;
L—leakage oil port;
X, Y—control oil ports.

6.1 A product nameplate should be set up in an obvious part of the hydraulic component, and the content of the nameplate should include:
—Name, model, factory number;
—Main technical parameters;
—Manufacturer name;
—Date of delivery.

6.7 The following contents should be clearly marked in words in a prominent position on the outer wall of the packaging box:
—Name, model;
—Quantity and gross weight;
—External dimensions (length, width, height) of the packaging box;
—Manufacturer name;
—Packing date;
—User name, address and station name;
—Transportation precautions or operation signs.
